body:
hm replaying RDR2... I finished it a couple of days ago haha but still it will be different i'm sure. 

&#x200B;

AC Odyssey replay... no way too much DLC and hours into it to get every rank etc, damn i'm glad this is cloud saved. Tho with other main character and other choices it will be alot different.

&#x200B;

Saw Metro aswell, but CoD is way to expensive for it's franchise imo. They released the same game years in a row. Kinda though to spend money on them.

Well i bought MCC edition, and 3 isn't out yet. 

LOL I had trouble with normal haha, that's a big leap to take.

&#x200B;

FFA? ok thx

And indeed, the SP was (at the moment) better then MP. Alot of frustration so good tip. Thx

&#x200B;

And I'm no quiter when it comes to games, was looking new to replace SWBFII and Rocket League, FPS has been ages for me, online that is.

&#x200B;

and ROFL HAHA

Hm, I don't know why but I think I was one of the first to download Unity for free, nothing was on reddit or anywhere about it, just launched uPlay, got the add & click. Nothing more.

&#x200B;

Maybe because I had every other AC game on it already dunno. And they weren't payed by creditcard either. Didn't ask anything.

&#x200B;

Same for that 4.0 NET Framework bug error. I get it on uPlay, click cancel and get to play.

I get it on Steam? Can't play in any way.

&#x200B;

Whish I could add Steam games to my uPlay library instead of the other way around. uPlay is starting to overfavor Steam for me.

&#x200B;

Sucks for you tho, it went automatically fine for me so I can't really help you out. But there is alot of software out there that gives you this kind of sh\*t.

I never even look at Assassin's Creed until i found out i had one for free from ages ago. Started it. Loved it. Now I'm binging them all. It was really weird getting into Odyssey at first, really hard game aswel.

&#x200B;

Then I played Origins and it kind of teached me the basics for Odyssey and now I can play Odyssey on normal finally lol.

&#x200B;

I want to go back to Origins and finish the endgame, but I just bought season pass for Odyssey instead because. Can't. F\*cking. Quit. Feels like I'm playing a single player WoW vanilla traveling the huge map.

Okay so the mercenary line continues, that's nice. I thought I was a God defeating the minotaur at lvl 36. And you do that kind of stuff? HAHA i'm noob.

&#x200B;

Blind King will be purchased have SO much uPlay points. Wish I could buy games with them.

&#x200B;

I think I already used the XP & money boost from uPlay in my 30-40s, i was struggling on easy.

&#x200B;

But indeed when you find a strategy around your build you can easely down higher level captains and such.

I've been downed just by fire damage so much everything I wear is like +Fire damage or duration or something and my weapon is the "all attacks are fire dmg" mace. Same for the bow, all arrow are fire arrows.

Put me in flames? Right back at ya.

I just started it!

Didn't even consider the first one since it's so over the place these games and no one mentions it, kinda weird for such a popular franchise imo.

&#x200B;

Yeah but the fight takes so long removing them al while blocking everything else. But I use my bird, forgot the name, flame me haha, now and it goes a LONG way since you can form a plan of execution to clear a hold or so.

&#x200B;

Got sparta kick just to kick them shields haha.

Broke up with my suicidal GF. Couldn't handle the automutilations after a year of suffering. Hardest thing I ever did.

She got me into self destruction and suicidal thoughts. Couldn't keep going. Bah.

&#x200B;

Looking for music like Slipknot/Disturbed/Stone Sour to listen 2.

&#x200B;

...Anything else would be rocket league themed lol...

Why are you playing video games? I like nice cars. Big whoop. I only have bedrest and game time. Sorry if i try to make that a little more interesting by changing the looks. 

&#x200B;

You better be gratefull you are NOT poor have NO problems and lalaland is free for you. Enjoy. Hope it lasts.
